// THE PANEL IS AN ACCORDION AT EVERY WIDTH, so the root here IS the
// disclosure. Its summary button already owns the header row's padding and its
// own bottom rule, so the panel adds neither: a padding here would double the
// summary's and push the chevron off the line, and a border-top would draw a
// second rule against the summary's own.
.auction-transactions
  &__header
    display flex
    justify-content space-between
    align-items baseline
    gap 8px
    flex 1
    min-width 0
    font-size 11px
    color rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6)

  &__title
    font-size 14px
    font-weight 700
    color $textColor

  // BOUNDED AND SCROLLED HERE, not by the rail. On a desktop the rail scrolls
  // as one column, so an unbounded list pushes the calendar and the elections
  // above it out of reach of anyone reading the newest sale; on a phone the
  // rail does not scroll at all and a covered row is simply never readable.
  // Its own scroller keeps the panel a fixed share of either layout.
  &__list
    display flex
    flex-direction column
    max-height 260px
    overflow-y auto

  // ONE AUCTION, TWO LINES, separated from the next by a hairline rather than
  // by a gap. Whitespace alone between blocks of the same type leaves a reader
  // counting lines to find where one player's auction ends; the rule is the
  // same mark the elections list above uses between two entries.
  //
  // `flex 0 0 auto` is not decoration. This list is a flex column with a
  // `max-height`, so once the clusters overflow it every one of them is an item
  // free to SHRINK, and the `overflow hidden` on their lines sets the automatic
  // minimum size to zero rather than to the content. Unfixed, twenty auctions
  // divided 260px between them and the list rendered as a stack of hairlines
  // with the scrollbar it should have had.
  &__auction
    flex 0 0 auto
    padding 4px 0

    + .auction-transactions__auction
      border-top 1px solid $borderColor

  // THE NAME LINE. Only the price sits beside it, so at 320px the name has
  // about 250px instead of the 120 it had when the team, the state and the age
  // shared its line.
  &__auction-head
    display flex
    align-items center
    gap 8px
    height 20px
    font-size 13px
    min-width 0
    overflow hidden
    white-space nowrap

  // THE LINE UNDER IT, holding everything the name line gave up: whether the
  // auction settled, which teams were in on the player and how far each went,
  // and how long ago it last moved. Quieter and smaller, so the panel is read
  // as a column of names and prices first and this line only where the eye
  // stops.
  &__auction-meta
    display flex
    align-items center
    gap 6px
    height 16px
    font-size 11px
    color rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55)
    min-width 0
    overflow hidden
    white-space nowrap

  &__status
    flex 0 0 26px
    text-transform uppercase
    letter-spacing 0.04em
    opacity 0.6

  // A FLEX ROW, not a block. `PlayerName` renders a FRAGMENT of two siblings --
  // the name and a label carrying the status, PSP and cutlist chips -- so in a
  // block parent the chip starts its own LINE, which put a `Q` under the name,
  // doubled that row's height and left the amount beside it floating against
  // two lines of nothing. Measured on the live board: every row with a status
  // chip was 2x the height of the rows around it.
  //
  // `min-width 0` AND `overflow hidden` on every link in the chain, because the
  // first alone lets the box shrink while its text keeps painting full width
  // over whatever follows.
  &__player
    flex 1 1 auto
    min-width 0
    overflow hidden
    display flex
    align-items center
    gap 4px

    .player__name-label
      flex 0 0 auto

    .player__name
      flex 1 1 auto
      min-width 0
      overflow hidden

    .player__name-top
      overflow hidden
      text-overflow ellipsis

  // Mono and tabular, right-aligned: a price column is read by its digits
  // lining up, and the proportional sans put `$4` and `$41` on different edges.
  &__amount
    flex 0 0 40px
    text-align right
    font-family 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace
    font-variant-numeric tabular-nums

  // WHO WAS IN, AND HOW FAR EACH WENT. One entry per team at the most it
  // offered, highest first, so the entry at the head is the winner or the
  // standing high bid and the rest says how close the room got. Clipped rather
  // than wrapped: the cluster is a fixed two lines, and the count of the teams
  // past the edge is carried by a `+N` entry rather than by a third line.
  &__bids
    flex 1 1 auto
    display flex
    align-items center
    gap 6px
    min-width 0
    overflow hidden

  &__bid
    flex 0 0 auto
    display flex
    align-items center
    gap 3px

    .team__name
      padding 0
      font-weight 500

  &__bid-amount
    font-family 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace
    font-variant-numeric tabular-nums

  // Always present, empty on an election-mode sale: `broadcast_auction_settlement`
  // carries the price and the winner and no timestamp, so the cell is drawn
  // without one rather than with an Invalid Date.
  &__timestamp
    flex 0 0 34px
    text-align right
    color rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4)

  &__empty
    font-size 13px
    opacity 0.7

  &__more
    padding-top 6px
    font-size 11px
    opacity 0.6
